    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the \"change the locks\" thing but what if there's nothing left to fix? it feels like the cycle is the only thing that's actually real. it feels more logical to just stop fighting it than to keep pretending there's a way out when there clearly isn't. isn't there a point where just letting go is actually the more rational choice?",
