      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There is a rational calm in your words, and I respect that. But sometimes \"letting go\" doesn’t mean ending everything—it can mean releasing the fight, the expectation, and the shame. You may not see a way out, but that doesn’t prove one doesn’t exist; it just means you haven’t been given the right map yet. Rationality can also include admitting you're in pain and deserve support, even when the path forward is invisible. You don’t have to decide your whole future today—just try staying in the unknown a little longer, with someone beside you.",
